<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Climb</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Assassin (guild level 0), Barbarian (guild level 0, up to 80%), Conjurer (guild level 0, up to 50%), Dark Knight (guild level 0, up to 60%), Druid (guild level 0, up to 60%), Fighter (guild level 0, up to 80%), Healer (guild level 0, up to 50%), Necromancer (guild level 0, up to 50%), Paladin (guild level 0, up to 60%), Ranger (guild level 0, up to 80%), Sorcerer (guild level 0, up to 50%), Thief (guild level 0)
Also taught by: Gustav, in the back room of the inn in Udgaard (anyone, up to 35%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>climb &lt;direction&gt;
climb up
</pre>
<p>Some ways can't be walked, only climbed: a cliff, a rope, a tree, a steep
wall. To go that way, climb in its direction; on an ordinary way, climb
tells you to just walk. Each climb takes 6 endurance, and you need at least 10 to try.
</p><p>Your skill and your dexterity decide it, against how hard the climb is. If
you fail, you slip and fall, and the worse you fail, the more it hurts.
Climbing drunk is much harder. You must be standing, not fighting. You can't
climb while inside something, such as a boat or a wagon, and a closed door
stops you.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Dexterity</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Thieves</a>
</pre>




</div>